  </div>
  <div style="text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 40px;">
    <p>SUNY College at Old Westbury is a selective public liberal arts college with more than <span data-field="number_of_students">{{ number_of_students }}</span> students studying in more than <span data-field="number_of_programs">{{ number_of_programs }}</span> undergraduate degree opportunities in its liberal arts and professional programs and <span data-field="number_of_graduate_programs">{{ number_of_graduate_programs }}</span> graduate programs in business, education and mental health counseling. On the College's <span data-field="campus_name">{{ campus_name }}</span>, students and faculty participate in an environment that demands academic excellence, fosters intercultural understanding, and endeavors to stimulate a passion for learning and a commitment to building a more just and sustainable world. The College boasts an <span data-field="accreditation_status">{{ accreditation_status }}</span> institution that prepares students for <span data-field="career_field">{{ career_field }}</span>, a student civic engagement program recognized by the Corporation for National Service, and the only state-accredited bachelor's degree program in Accounting offered by SUNY in the metropolitan New York area.</p>
  </div>

