<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 40px;">
    <h3 style="font-size: 16pt;">REGISTRATION INSTRUCTIONS FOR SUMMER 2020</h3>
    <div style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">
      <span data-field="link_registration">{{ link_registration }}</span>
    </div>
    <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt;">Instructions to enroll or drop courses.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h4 style="font-weight: bold;">REGISTRATION FOR SUMMER 2020</h4>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">New Students: To register for summer, students who have never attended SUNY Old Westbury must use the "Quick Admit" form at the SUNY Old Westbury website. Non-Degree Programs or Old Westbury Web site under Admissions, Non-Degree Programs or Continuing Education.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">For more information, visit <span data-field="website_url">{{ website_url }}</span>.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h4 style="font-weight: bold;">FINANCIAL AID</h4>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Financial aid is available to students enrolled for six or more credits as a regular student in an eligible program. The types of assistance available to students include Federal Pell Grant, Federal Supplemental Educational Opportunity Grant, SUNY Grant, and private loans. Students must complete the financial aid application form and provide financial need documentation. For further details, Financial Aid Advisers are available in the Financial Aid Office of Financial Aid, Campus Center, Student Service Center, Head Office, and the Registrar's Office. Students should submit their process of filing financial aid paperwork for the summer in early March.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h4 style="font-weight: bold;">REGISTRATION FOR TR I O CREDITS</h4>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Summer 2020 registration begins March 18, 2020.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Registration on the WEB for Continuing Students.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Instructions to enroll or drop courses.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">For more information, visit <span data-field="link_trio">{{ link_trio }}</span>.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h4 style="font-weight: bold;">GRADING POLICY</h4>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The grading system for all students is based on a letter grade scale, A=90-100%, B=80-89%, C=70-79%, D=60-69%, F=0-59%. Students who remain on the roster after the Add/Drop period receive one grade.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h4 style="font-weight: bold;">CREDIT/NO CREDIT OPTIONS</h4>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">For courses offered for credit, the student must register for the course. For courses offered for no credit, the student must register for the course. Students who register for a course for credit but do not attend the course will be charged a fee. Students who register for a course for no credit but do not attend the course will not be charged a fee.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">If this prospectus is not followed, a grade of no credit will not be received at all. If grading is official, it is assigned to the student's record. If the student does not attend the course, a grade of no credit will be assigned for the course.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h4 style="font-weight: bold;">TRANSCRIPT</h4>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Transcripts are available for viewing online at the Old Westbury Student Portal. If you intend to transfer to another institution, you should request an official transcript. An official transcript is a sealed document sent directly from the College to the receiving institution. Students can request an official transcript through the Registrar's Office.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

